🛡️ Penetration Test Report: Internal HR Portal

Target: hr-portal.internal.corp

Scope: User login functionality, password reset, and session handling.

1. Executive Summary

This report details findings from the Broken Authentication testing phase against the internal HR Portal. The primary finding is a Critical Risk due to the complete lack of rate limiting on the /login endpoint, enabling an attacker to perform an infinite, low-velocity, online brute-force attack against any user account.

Key Findings Identified:

Critical Risk: Missing rate limiting, leading to successful brute-forcing of credentials.

Low Risk: Weak password policy allows short, simple, or dictionary passwords.

The exploitation of this flaw allows an unauthenticated attacker to gain access to sensitive employee data (salaries, performance reviews, PII) stored within the HR system. 

2. Methodology

Testing focused exclusively on the user login and session management processes using Burp Suite to analyze response times and retry limits.

