4. Immediate Remediation Recommendations

Implement Rate Limiting (AUTH-001): Implement a robust, IP-based, and session-based rate-limiting mechanism on the /login endpoint. This should block requests exceeding 5 failed attempts per IP address/session within a 5-minute window.

Implement Account Lockout (AUTH-001): After a defined number of failed attempts (e.g., 5), lock the target account for a set duration (e.g., 30 minutes) or require manual administrator intervention/email verification to unlock.

Enforce Strong Password Policy (AUTH-002): Implement mandatory password requirements (minimum 12 characters, requiring mixing of uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and special symbols). Utilize a common password blocklist to prevent dictionary attacks.
